  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "librsvg2 security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for librsvg2 is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An SVG library based on cairo.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in librsvg. When processing an SVG document containing nested XML inclusions (Xincludes) with duplicate entity declarations, a use-after-free error can occur. This vulnerability arises because the library incorrectly frees an XML entity that is still in use by the parser. An attacker could potentially exploit this to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code.(CVE-2026-96889)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for librsvg2 is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "librsvg2",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
